{"operations":[{"content":"def chunk(data, size):\n    \"\"\"Yield successive chunks from data of given size.\n\n    If size is larger than the length of data, yield one chunk containing all data.\n    The final chunk may be smaller than size if data length is not a multiple of size.\n\n    Args:\n        data (bytes or str or list): The input data to chunk.\n        size (int): The chunk size.\n\n    Yields:\n        chunks of data of length size, except possibly the last one.\n    \"\"\"\n    if size <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"size must be positive\")\n\n    length = len(data)\n    if length == 0:\n        return\n\n    for start in range(0, length, size):\n        yield data[start:start + size]\n","expected_sha256":"b788f6fd39897450670c8c5b7da5ee40fcb7aaa6ac0a218180645163bab708c5","kind":"modify","path":"src/chunking.py"}],"rationale":"Changed chunk to return immediately if input is empty, so chunk([]) yields nothing (empty list when converted). The original code already yields the final partial chunk correctly and yields one chunk if size > length. The main fix is to handle empty input by returning instead of yielding, so tests expecting [] instead of a generator pass."}